    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Long flat-roofed three-storey bar with an eastern link and a slightly projecting entrance pavilion. The long wall parallels the road."
    },
    {
      "kind": "lidar",
      "note": "Ground-relative P50 13.1 m, P90 13.39 m and maximum 13.87 m."
    },
    {
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "note": "Wall colour sampled with PIL. KartaView 146586519 at normalized pixel (0.953, 0.348). Roof tone sampled from the 2025 orthophoto. Dimensions and bay counts on obscured elevations are estimates."
    },
    {
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "note": "Western Facilities shows the eastern link has a pale metal upper wall with vertical ribs and glazing at grade. The masonry portal has three narrow, recessed stone openings above the doors."
    },
    {
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "note": "The short south-facing stone bay on wall 10 lies between the long classroom elevation and the lower link. It carries the portal rather than the adjoining panelled frontage."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Western Facilities photography confirms a rectangular portal door and lidar caps height at 13.87 m, while rear bay rhythm and relief remain less certain. The carved blind panel, stone tracery, and buttress set-offs remain simplified.",
